WEBVTT

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:05.030
The festival of dreams
to crown the strongest Pokémon Trainer...

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:08.910
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.030
The second match of the semifinals:

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:16.120
The Champion of Sinnoh, Shirona,
versus the first Champion of Alola, Satoshi.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.870
Their 6v6 full battle has begun.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.830
Let the battle begin!

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:22.880
Draco Meteor!

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.470
Surprise Attack!

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:41.230
Employing skillful Pokémon switches centered
around Mikaruge, Shirona had Satoshi at her mercy.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:46.070
Kairyu, Gänger,
and even Pikachu were knocked out.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:49.860
Shirona has four Pokémon left.
Satoshi has three.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.740
How will Satoshi fight back
with one less Pokémon?

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.970
Pikachu, you really gave it your all!

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.350
You watch from here.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:02.120
Satoshi has three Pokémon left.
Ms. Shirona has four.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:05.790
That gap is huge.
Ms. Shirona is just too incredible.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.170
‘Scu-‘scu-‘scu-‘scuse us!

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.380
Hey! Brat boy!

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:14.090
Where’d all your steam
from the first round go?!

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.800
Don’t you dare
let us down, meow!

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:28.150
Neither of them have used
Daimax or Mega Evolution yet.

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:29.770
They’re both reading each other.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.320
The question of when to use them
is the key to deciding this battle.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.910
Competitor Shirona and Competitor Satoshi
are both ready to send out a new Pokémon.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.580
Uonoragon, I choose you!

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.830
Dance in the heavens, Gaburias!

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:04.350
This time, they’ve both sent out
Pokémon with the Dragon type!

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:06.060
Gaburias...

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:09.980
Is this where she brings out
the Mega Evolution?

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.820
All I can do is dive right in!

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:16.860
Ice Fang!

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.000
Draw it closer
and use Dragon Claw!

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:42.800
So fast...

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.310
Dragon moves are super effective!

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:47.810
Stealth Rock!

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:59.700
Sharp rocks were scattered
across the field!

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.860
Return, Gaburias!

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:02.820
Wha—?!

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.830
Go, Roserade!

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.840
Competitor Shirona
recalls yet again!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.590
Huh? It’s not burned...

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:19.920
It took Gänger’s
Will-O-Wisp earlier...

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.180
Hold on...

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.600
Could that Roserade...?

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:29.810
Its ability is Natural Cure.

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:34.860
By returning to its Monster Ball,
it recovers from poison or burns.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:37.650
So that’s why you
returned it before...

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.570
Drat!

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.490
Then I’ll... I’ll...

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.580
All right! Let’s do this!

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.870
Jaw Bite!

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.000
Poison Jab!

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:14.100
Wow! Both sides took damage!

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.730
Oh, no!

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:24.610
Looks like Poison Jab’s effect is slowly
eating away at Uonoragon’s stamina!

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:26.700
That’s not good.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:27.620
No...

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.790
What’s going on?

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.460
It’s angry that
it was poisoned, meow.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.760
It’s saying “I’ll take down
that Roserade myself!”, meow.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.920
Huh? Wow, it’s got serious guts!

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.930
Go get her, Uonoragon!

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.140
Leaf Storm!

00:06:58.110 --> 00:06:59.320
Dragon Dive!

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.830
And it’s over!

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:23.970
Roserade is unable to battle!

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:26.130
All right!

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:31.850
Return, Roserade!

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:35.980
You fought well.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:39.400
Despite its suffering,
Uonoragon pulls out a win!

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.320
But the effects of the poison
still linger!

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:42.940
Return—

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.160
Oh! It’s not going back...

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.870
Got it, Uonoragon.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.660
You still wanna battle!

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:55.910
Give it all you’ve got!

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:01.170
Competitor Satoshi
will continue with Uonoragon!

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:03.300
What a hard worker!

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.340
How brave...

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:08.680
Uonoragon...
We’re with you, meow!

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:14.350
You consider how Pokémon feel,
so it was only natural.

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:18.440
But that could also
give me a chance at another win...

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:21.860
Graceful spirit of water...

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:23.360
Milokaross!

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:31.370
Competitor Shirona sends in Milokaross,
who played a big role in the first round!

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.410
I’ve gotta end this quick,
for Uonoragon!

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.830
Dragon Dive!

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.460
Charm Voice!

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:52.600
It’s a Fairy move,
super effective on Uonoragon!

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.810
Hang in there, Uonoragon!

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:03.940
Milokaross! Do it!

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.950
And it’s trapped!

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:21.330
Iron Head!

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.580
Jaw Bite!

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:43.770
Uonoragon...

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:48.280
Uonoragon is unable to battle!

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:52.280
Another victory for
Competitor Shirona!

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:59.160
You really did your best.
Thank you!

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.670
Uonoragon’s last attack...

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:06.130
That must’ve dealt
a heavy blow to Milokaross, too.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:10.170
Yeah.
He’s set up his next play.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.550
Amazing, meow...

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:15.550
That’s Daimax bravery!

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:20.100
You fought well!
You’ve left me in tears!

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:26.810
Come on, Negigaknight!

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:32.150
The Stealth Rock?!

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:37.580
Stealth Rock activates!
Negigaknight takes damage from being switched in!

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:42.830
I’ve gotta do something...

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.390
Of course! That’s it!

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:04.520
Negigaknight!
Let’s clear the field with just one move!

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.360
Brutal Swing your shield!

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.290
Go, go, go!

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:26.920
I can’t believe it...

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:33.420
The shield is spinning at an incredible speed,
destroying the sharp Stealth Rocks one after another!

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:35.170
Is that even possible?!

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:36.300
Now <i>this</i> is it!

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.180
That’s Satoshi for you!

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:41.680
He really does the unbelievable!

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:45.180
<i>Go, go, go!</i>

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:54.030
Hydro Pump!

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:02.910
Consecutive Cut!

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:11.000
Iron Head!

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:28.810
Iron Head gets blocked!
Consecutive Cut hits its mark!

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:30.690
Charm Voice!

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:36.690
Star Assault!

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:46.410
Negigaknight is enduring
the Charm Voice!

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:49.710
<i>Go!</i>

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:04.850
Milokaross is unable to battle!

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:11.600
Plunging in with a fearless attack,
Negigaknight snatches a win for Satoshi!

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.480
You did it, Negigaknight!

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:18.360
<i>All right!</i>

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:20.860
Now they’re both
down to two Pokémon.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:24.490
The playing field’s even again...

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:30.160
Leave the rest to me, Milokaross.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.170
You can have a nice rest.

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:36.500
Your Stealth Rock counter
was marvelous.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:40.420
Our battle has lit a fire in me!

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:44.140
All the more reason why
I want to win this.

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:49.850
To win,
and battle Dande in the final!

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:52.850
We’re gonna be the ones winning,
Ms. Shirona.

00:13:56.320 --> 00:14:00.070
With this battle,
I’m gonna surpass you!

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:05.870
I call on you again, Gaburias!

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:15.330
Is she going to Mega Evolve this time?

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:35.850
Let’s move! Consecutive Cut!

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:41.150
Scale Shot!

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:49.700
Negigaknight cuts down the Scale Shot
and charges in!

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.950
Dragon Claw!

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:01.840
Detect!

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:08.510
Detect succeeds!
Gaburias’s claws rend the air!

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:09.760
Star Assault!

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:13.770
Draco Meteor!

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:47.130
Both sides take heavy damage...

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:49.640
What will happen next?!

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:09.990
Negigaknight!

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.250
Negigaknight is unable to battle!

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.510
Negigaknight has passed out
still standing!

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:31.970
Refusing to hit the ground, even in defeat...
What a paragon of chivalry!

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:34.640
Return, Negigaknight!

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:40.350
Thank you, Negigaknight.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:45.030
Competitor Satoshi
is down to just one Pokémon.

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:46.490
Return, Gaburias.

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:47.490
What?!

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:50.110
Another switch?

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:54.280
I really expected her
to use Mega Evolution.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.250
She has a different idea.

00:16:57.290 --> 00:16:59.040
This is all I have left!

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:00.500
Let’s use our full power!

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:03.000
Lucario! I choose you!

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:09.550
Competitor Satoshi’s sixth Pokémon,
and his last, is Lucario!

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:12.430
Aceburn?

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:14.680
You mean you want to
cheer on Lucario...?

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:19.390
Lucario!
Aceburn’s watching, too!

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:21.270
Give it your all!

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.700
Aceburn...

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:33.910
Lucario!

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:37.120
Let’s make Aceburn proud!

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:42.170
Togekiss,
I call on you again!

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:50.920
That powerful flinching combo brought about
by its ability, Heaven’s Blessings, and Air Slash...

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:57.220
I wonder how Satoshi
intends to handle it.

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:01.390
Competitor Satoshi’s
last Pokémon is Lucario!

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:04.980
How will they measure up
against Competitor Shirona and Togekiss?

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.150
Bullet Punch!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.200
Air Slash!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:25.210
Amazing!
It’s blowing away the Air Slash!

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:29.920
Lucario’s skillful Bullet Punches
block the Flying move!

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:35.680
Jump, Lucario!

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:48.940
All right! It felt that!

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.830
As I thought, you’re in perfect sync.

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:03.210
A move born from the bond
that your Aura forged.

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:04.830
I’m not done!

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:05.920
Aura Sphere!

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:09.460
Air Slash!

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:21.470
Air Slash blows away Lucario
and the Aura Sphere!

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:31.610
You okay, Lucario?!

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:45.790
Oh? What’s wrong, Lucario?

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:48.380
Has it made you flinch?

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.380
Lucario!

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.550
This is just like with Pikachu!

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:55.090
No, Lucario will be fine.

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:55.880
Huh?

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:02.560
One more Air Slash!

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.310
Bullet Punch!

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:11.690
He’s not flinching!

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:16.570
This time,
he completely repels the Air Slash!

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.320
Good job, Lucario!

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:24.830
What incredible willpower.

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:37.840
Return, Togekiss!

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:40.340
Huh?!

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:43.100
What? Yet another recall?

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.850
A Daimax band!

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:56.490
No! She’s not recalling it!

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:01.240
Tower over all, white wings!

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:08.290
Daimax Togekiss!

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:28.430
Let’s do this, Lucario!

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:37.440
With Togekiss Daimaxing,
Shirona and Satoshi’s bout only becomes fiercer.

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:41.400
Will Satoshi be able to find a way to
take it down?

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:10.870
<i>Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament News!</i>

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:13.790
And so, the semifinals continue!

00:23:13.790 --> 00:23:17.500
How are you going to deal with
that supersized Togekiss, Competitor Satoshi?

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:18.590
Huh?

00:23:18.590 --> 00:23:21.590
But Competitor Shirona
still has Gaburias, too, meow.

00:23:21.590 --> 00:23:23.550
What?!
Then he’s <i>doomed!</i>

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:24.760
Oh, no!

00:23:24.760 --> 00:23:27.590
<i>Go for it, go for it, brat boy!</i>

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:30.390
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:32.430
The Semifinals IV - “Shock”

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:34.350
Let’s all tune in, meow!
